Hunk A — backend/alembic/env.py:20 (one-line shape as the packet expected):
    -    fileConfig(config.config_file_name)
    +    fileConfig(config.config_file_name, disable_existing_loggers=False)
  A1 truth (1 world, no branching): prior behaviour `fileConfig(ini)` used the
  logging.config default `disable_existing_loggers=True`, which on every alembic
  config load set `app.api.v1.health.disabled = True` process-wide; under
  full-suite ordering a migration test ran first, so the health logger was dead
  by the time test_health_reports_database_failure ran -> caplog.text == ''.
  `disable_existing_loggers=False` keeps the ini's own config while not
  disabling unrelated existing loggers.

Hunk B — backend/app/services/dedup.py (annotation + import only; no statement
  change): `from sqlalchemy import Row` added; parameter annotation changed
  from `list[tuple[Observation, Asset]] | None` to
  `list[Row[tuple[Observation, Asset]]] | None`, which is the true type of
  `db.query(Observation, Asset).all()`. `for row, asset in phash_rows` already
  unpacked a Row at runtime; only the annotation now tells the truth.

